{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLHarmony"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharmony\/init(id:chord:frame:offset:footnote:level:staff:kind:printsobject:printsframe:arrangement:position:font:color:placement:system:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"chord"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/Chord-swift.struct","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLHarmonyV5ChordV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Chord"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = [], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"frame"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLFrameV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLFrame"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"offset"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOffset","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLOffsetV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLOffset"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"footnote"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFormattedText","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLFormattedTextV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLFormattedText"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"level"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"staff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaff","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLStaffV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStaff"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/Kind-swift.enum","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLHarmonyV4KindO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Kind"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"printsObject"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"printsFrame"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"arrangement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmonyArrangement","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL21MXLHarmonyArrangementO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLHarmonyArrangement"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":" = MXLPosition(), "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"font"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLFont"},{"kind":"text","text":" = MXLFont(), "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"placement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"system"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemRelation","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSystemRelation"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil)"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that specifies an id reference."}]}],"name":"id"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A harmony element can contain many stacked chords (e.g. V of II). A sequence of harmony-chord groups is used for this type of secondary function, where V of II would be represented by a harmony-chord with a 5 numeral followed by a harmony-chord with a 2 numeral."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"chord"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fretboard diagram to be printed with this harmony."}]}],"name":"frame"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Indicates where this harmony will appear relative to the current musical location, in divisions."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"offset"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The footnote element specifies editorial information that appears in footnotes in the printed score. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}]}],"name":"footnote"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The level element specifies editorial information for different MusicXML elements. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"level"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff element is defined within a group due to its use by both notes and direction elements."}]}],"name":"staff"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Differentiates whether this harmony is explicit, implied, or an alternate analysis, when alternate harmonies are possible."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"kind"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether to print an object (e.g. a note or a rest). Defaults to "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if not specified."}]}],"name":"printsObject"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether to print a frame or fretboard diagram for this harmony."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"printsFrame"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Specifies how multiple harmony-chord groups are arranged relative to each other."}]}],"name":"arrangement"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"position"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"font"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"color"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"placement"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The system-relation attribute group distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the particular part where the element appears.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"system"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"chord"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLHarmonyV5ChordV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Chord"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"frame"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLFrameV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLFrame"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"offset"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLOffsetV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLOffset"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"footnote"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLFormattedTextV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLFormattedText"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"level"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"staff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLStaffV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStaff"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLHarmonyV4KindO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Kind"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"printsObject"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"printsFrame"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"arrangement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL21MXLHarmonyArrangementO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLHarmonyArrangement"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"font"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLFont"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"placement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"system"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSystemRelation"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"role":"symbol","title":"init(id:chord:frame:offset:footnote:level:staff:kind:printsObject:printsFrame:arrangement:position:font:color:placement:system:)","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLHarmonyV2id5chord5frame6offset8footnote5level5staff4kind12printsObject0L5Frame11arrangement8position4font5color9placement6systemACSSSg_SayAC5ChordVGAA8MXLFrameVSgAA9MXLOffsetVSgAA16MXLFormattedTextVSgAA8MXLLevelVSgAA8MXLStaffVSgAC4KindOSgSbSgA14_AA0C11ArrangementOSgAA11MXLPositionVAA7MXLFontVAA8MXLColorVSgAA13MXLAboveBelowOSgAA17MXLSystemRelationOSgtcfc","roleHeading":"Initializer","symbolKind":"init"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/init(id:chord:frame:offset:footnote:level:staff:kind:printsObject:printsFrame:arrangement:position:font:color:placement:system:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaff":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaff","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaff","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLStaff","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaff","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaff","abstract":[{"text":"The staff element is defined within a group due to its use by both notes and direction elements.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"title":"MXLFont","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemRelation":{"title":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The system-relation type distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the particular","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part where the element appears. A value of only-top indicates that the element should appear only on the top","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part of the current system. A value of also-top indicates that the element should appear on both the current","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part and the top part of the current system. If this value appears in a score, when parts are created the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element should only appear once in this part, not twice. A value of none indicates that the element is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"associated only with the current part, not with the system.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemRelation","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemrelation"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLevel":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLLevel","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLevel","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllevel","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The level type is used to specify editorial information for different MusicXML elements. The content contains"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifying and\/or descriptive text about the editorial status of the parent element."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"title":"MXLPosition"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarmony/Chord-swift.struct":{"title":"MXLHarmony.Chord","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Chord"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A harmony element can contain many stacked chords (e.g. V of II). A sequence of harmony-chord groups is used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for this type of secondary function, where V of II would be represented by a harmony-chord with a 5 numeral","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"followed by a harmony-chord with a 2 numeral.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/Chord-swift.struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Chord"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharmony\/chord-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOffset":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloffset","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOffset","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOffset"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An offset is represented in terms of divisions, and indicates where the direction will appear relative to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"current musical location. The current musical location is always within the current measure, even at the end","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of a measure.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOffset"}],"title":"MXLOffset"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAboveBelow":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlabovebelow","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The above-below type is used to indicate whether one element appears above or below another element.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"title":"MXLAboveBelow"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFrame":{"abstract":[{"text":"The frame type represents a frame or fretboard diagram used together with a chord symbol. The representation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is based on the NIFF guitar grid with additional information. The frame type’s unplayed attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"what to display above a string that has no associated frame-note element. Typical values are x and the empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string. If the attribute is not present, the display of the unplayed string is application-defined.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlframe","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame","kind":"symbol","title":"MXLFrame","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFrame","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFrame","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarmony/Kind-swift.enum":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/Kind-swift.enum","title":"MXLHarmony.Kind","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharmony\/kind-swift.enum","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The harmony-type type differentiates different types of harmonies when alternate harmonies are possible."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Explicit harmonies have all note present in the music; implied have some notes missing but implied;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alternate represents alternate analyses."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarmonyArrangement":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLHarmonyArrangement","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharmonyarrangement","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmonyArrangement","title":"MXLHarmonyArrangement","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLHarmonyArrangement","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The harmony-arrangement type indicates how stacked chords and bass notes are displayed within a harmony"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. The vertical value specifies that the second element appears below the first. The horizontal value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies that the second element appears to the right of the first. The diagonal value specifies that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second element appears both below and to the right of the first."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFormattedText":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The formatted-text type represents a text element with text-formatting attributes."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"MXLFormattedText","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFormattedText"}],"title":"MXLFormattedText","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFormattedText","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlformattedtext","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarmony":{"title":"MXLHarmony","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct